				<text x="32" y="356" font-size="16" fill="#475569">Fix only what's off</text>
				<line x1="180" y1="374" x2="180" y2="396" stroke="#0F172A" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#in-sp-arr)"/>
				<rect x="16" y="400" width="328" height="100" rx="6" fill="#fff" stroke="#E2E8F0"/>
				<text x="32" y="428" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.5" fill="#64748b">NEXT</text>
				<text x="32" y="456" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="#0F172A">Next step suggested</text>
				<text x="32" y="484" font-size="16" fill="#475569">175 automations watch</text>
				<rect x="16" y="520" width="328" height="76" rx="6" fill="#0F172A"/>
				<text x="180" y="550" font-size="16" font-weight="600" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">AI takes on the typing.</text>
				<text x="180" y="574" font-size="16" font-weight="600" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">People make the calls.</text>
				</g>
			</svg>
			<figcaption id="input-figure-caption">AI writes the record and a person only checks it. From each saved record, the next step comes up on its own.</figcaption>
		</figure>
		<header class="problems-overview">
			<div class="why-head">
				<p class="section-eyebrow">Common Problems</p>
				<h2>Three months after rollout,<br /><span class="text-emph">the team is back in spreadsheets.</span></h2>
				<p class="section-lead">The number one reason a CRM stops being used is the effort of entering data.</p>
			</div>
			<blockquote class="problem-example">
				<p>Meeting notes stay in a notebook and on a phone.<br />Before Monday's meeting, someone is <strong>pulling the numbers together in a spreadsheet by hand</strong>.</p>
			</blockquote>
		</header>
