					<div class="problem-response"><p class="problem-topic">With Revenue CRM</p><p>{item.answer}</p></div>
				</article>
			))}
		</div>
		<p class="problems-more"><a href="/en/crm/features/" class="btn btn--outline-primary">See all {featureCount()} features →</a></p>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== FOUNDER (why it was built. Facts the founder has stated only) ===================== -->
<section class="founder" aria-labelledby="founder-title">
	<div class="container founder-inner">
		<figure class="founder-photo">
			<img src="/images/common/seiko-yamaguchi-2026b.jpg" alt="Seiko Yamaguchi, Founder, Consilegy LLC" width="720" height="864" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
		</figure>
		<div class="founder-body">
			<p class="section-eyebrow">Founder's Note</p>
			<h2 id="founder-title">Why I built Revenue CRM.</h2>
			<p>Over eight years, I have helped more than 40 companies roll out CRM systems. Right after rollout, every company is excited. A few months later, data entry stops and the team drifts back to spreadsheets. I have watched that happen again and again.</p>
			<p>The people who stopped using it were not the problem. The problem was a design that made people adapt to the system.</p>
			<p>Revenue CRM is designed around the system adapting to people. AI drafts the records, and people check them and make the calls. Each business gets screens and automations that fit what it manages. Not people fitting the system, but a system that fits people. That is the idea behind this product.</p>
			<p class="founder-sign">Seiko Yamaguchi, Founder, Consilegy LLC</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

